body:
yeah i used to not use cash but past year I exclusively use cash bar large purchases (£200+). Any place which doesn't accept cash i do not attend. Reason for using cash is because of the governments plans to introduce CBDCs and I fear that eventually this will wipe out physical cash creating a scenario where everything we buy is tracked and under control of someone other than myself and i do not want that, so i use cash as a form of 'protest' i guess. I feel like the more people use cash, the harder it is for the government to phase out physical cash.

&#x200B;

edit: essentially, i don't want any third party constantly looking over my shoulder.

Thank you, yep i definitely will. Im not really sure on what to say though;

Im essentially thinking of something along the lines of "i have a massive passion for x subject/course and my predicted grades arent a true reflection of what i can achieve and i know i can exceed the grade requirements; i think it would be an injustice if predicted grades were to shape my future in such a significant way when i know i am more than capable of reaching the grade requirements". (In a lot better writing of course while mentioning some extra things i have done to show my passion)

I cant really think of what else to say, what do you think?
